# The app's settings. A production build checks them (`npm run build:prod`, `next build`, the
# image's build), and a production server reads and checks them again as it starts (`npm run
# start:prod`, `next start`, the image). Both stop while one marked "required"
# is missing or malformed, or an optional server, relay, indexer or metadata URL is malformed
# (lib/deployment.ts, productionProblems), or while one names a server that will not do or cannot
# be asked. `next dev` and the devnet take defaults instead. Copy this to web/.env.production and
# fill it in. Node 22 or later: the checks reach each server over the runtime's own WebSocket.
#
# A build made with no network may set SOLIDPOOL_OFFLINE_BUILD=1 to leave the servers to the start,
# which always asks them.

# Required: the network a fresh page opens on, mainnet or chipnet, written exactly so, and one this
# deployment offers (below). A person can choose another offered network in Settings; the choice
# stays in their browser. `local` is the devnet, which a production server runs only for a test
# deployment with DEVNET_ENABLED=1.
POOL_NETWORK=mainnet

# ---- Mainnet and chipnet ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# A production server offers each of the two that its settings set anything for, and only those.
# A network it offers needs all four settings marked "required" below, or the build and the server
# stop and name what it lacks; leave all of a network's empty and it is not offered. Each setting
# carries its network's name: MAINNET_ for mainnet, CHIPNET_ for chipnet.
#
# The same names without the prefix (TRUSTLESS_FULCRUM_URL, TRUSTLESS_BROADCAST_URL, BCH_FACTORY,
# TOKEN_FACTORY and INDEXER_URL) name POOL_NETWORK's network, as they did when a deployment named
# only that one, and as the indexer reads its factories. Where both are set they must name the same
# server, factory or indexer, or production stops.
#
# Each network's settings:
# - _TRUSTLESS_FULCRUM_URL and _TRUSTLESS_BROADCAST_URL, required: two Fulcrum servers of that
#   network, which every browser reads directly over an encrypted WebSocket (wss://). The first
#   serves reads and deposits; the second, from another operator, takes withdrawals, so neither
#   sees a wallet and its withdrawal together. Each runs Fulcrum 1.10 or later: a production build
#   and server refuse one older, or one that follows another chain, and the server reads the
#   network's factories through the first.
# - _BCH_FACTORY and _TOKEN_FACTORY, required: the categories of that network's BCH and token pool
#   factories, 64 hex digits each, which the page indexes pools from when it reads the chain
#   itself. deployments/<network>.json names them under `factories`, and
#   web/deployments/<network>.json, once it names them, must agree. The indexer takes the same two.
# - _INDEXER_URL, optional: that network's indexer (indexer/README.md), for a fast first paint.
#   This server reads its pool list and every browser its archive, so it must be a public https://
#   URL.
#
# Before each network had names of its own, the other network's servers were MAINNET_ or
# CHIPNET_FULCRUM_URL and _BROADCAST_URL. Nothing reads those now, and production refuses them,
# naming the setting that replaced each.

# ---- Mainnet ----
# The factories are those of deployments/mainnet.json.
MAINNET_TRUSTLESS_FULCRUM_URL=wss://electrum.imaginary.cash:50004
MAINNET_TRUSTLESS_BROADCAST_URL=wss://electroncash.dk:50004
MAINNET_BCH_FACTORY=d8db78466ca0636f0f1ab902aa9efa8833ab18345011faf8dc3a9e2cb53c26c7
MAINNET_TOKEN_FACTORY=da5397afd56f2ff9c732699c0849133b0d4b4256a2fcd5848c60bac678185d21
MAINNET_INDEXER_URL=https://mainnet.solidpool.cash

# ---- Chipnet ----
# The factories are those of deployments/chipnet.json.
CHIPNET_TRUSTLESS_FULCRUM_URL=wss://chipnet.imaginary.cash:50004
CHIPNET_TRUSTLESS_BROADCAST_URL=wss://chipnet.bch.ninja:50004
CHIPNET_BCH_FACTORY=b6ebe8575e5c9f2dbc193486245cfbe1a02dd32a8648127eb11bc28b58047ecb
CHIPNET_TOKEN_FACTORY=cf0006fa6a53a4309293cb4bb548f9d2f5a5da0ec2bf69e5c02fa817dd443bc8
CHIPNET_INDEXER_URL=https://chipnet.solidpool.cash

# ---- Devnet ----
# The local service's own chain, for debugging. `next dev` offers it, and a production build only
# for a test deployment with POOL_NETWORK=local and DEVNET_ENABLED=1: a mainnet or chipnet server
# refuses it, and so does `npm run start:prod`. Its factories are the ones the service writes to
# deployments/local.json (DEPLOYMENT_FILE), and a page reads its chain from the service
# (SERVICE_URL), at DEVNET_FULCRUM_URL where a browser reaches the service at another address than
# this server does. None of the settings above applies to it.
DEVNET_ENABLED=0
# SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788
# DEVNET_FULCRUM_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8788
# DEPLOYMENT_FILE=../deployments/local.json

# ---- Every network ----

# Required: this deployment's WalletConnect Cloud project id, 32 hex digits, with the
# deployment's domain allowed in that project. `next dev` and the devnet use a shared public one.
WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=3fd234b8e2cd0e1da4bc08a0011bbf64
# WALLETCONNECT_RELAY_URL=wss://relay.walletconnect.org

# Token metadata. The page asks this app's own registry (public/bcmr) first, then this service,
# Paytaca's index by default, and shows what the service says as unverified. Only for a token
# neither has does it walk the token's authchain on chain, and only that answer is verified. A
# marketplace-style service is accepted too.
BCMR_SERVICE_URL=https://bcmr.paytaca.com

# Next's anonymous telemetry stays off. The project's scripts and next.config.ts set this; set it
# wherever else Next runs.
NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1

# The prover assets are served from public/prover by default. Point these elsewhere to
# serve them from a CDN; the browser checks their SHA-256 before using them.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CIRCUIT_URL=/prover/withdraw.json
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PROVING_KEY_URL=/prover/withdraw_proving_key.bin

# Required: the public https:// origin this deployment is served at, which link previews point to.
SITE_URL=https://solidpool.cash

# Required: a public https:// address that serves the exact source of this build, such as its
# commit or tag in a public repository. The page as served is conveyed under the GPL-3.0, and it
# links every browser here: the build bakes the value into the page. Build and run with the same
# value, since a server started with another stops, and keep it available for as long as the build
# is served (PRODUCTION.md). `next dev` and the devnet need none.
# SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/<owner>/<repository>/tree/<commit>
SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/mainnet-pat/solidpool

# Where `npm run start:prod` serves the app: every interface, port 8787, unless set.
# APP_HOST=0.0.0.0
# APP_PORT=8787
